Changes in this fork (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b))

This is a fork of TensorFold 1.0.2 (upstream commit f8fe17d) by BertholomusAI (Albert Lee,
https://github.com/bertholomus), Copyright 2026. It adds the dsv41 model family for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on TensorFold
1.0's native Zig engine, tensor-parallel over two NVIDIA GB10 nodes, with image input. TensorFold's text above,
LICENSE, the upstream files in LICENSES/ and the upstream sections of THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md are unchanged.

Added:
  zig/src/families/dsv41/                  the model family (model, prompt and decode paths, kernels' launches,
                                           the RDMA ring, the follower rank tf-dsv41-lanes, the vision tower)
  zig/kernels/cuda/dsv41/                  the family's CUDA kernels
  zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig, tool_parse_test.zig   DeepSeek-V4.1's DSML tool calls
  tools/dsv41-zig/                         recording and comparison tools, and ATTRIBUTION.md
  LICENSES/Pillow-MIT-CMU.txt, LICENSES/PyTorch-BSD-3-Clause.txt, LICENSES/CUTLASS-BSD-3-Clause.txt
  A "DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on CUDA (Zig)" section in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, and a fork note at the top of README.md.

Modified upstream files:
  zig/build/cuda.zig               build steps for the dsv41 family, its kernels, tf-dsv41-lanes and the vision tower
  zig/src/core/engine_api.zig      image spans and an engine's reasoning-effort numbers in the engine API
  zig/src/core/lane_host.zig       images through the lane host; a request the pool cannot hold yet waits for a
                                   stream to end instead of failing
  zig/src/core/lanes/stream.zig    a stream's image spans
  zig/src/cuda/aot.zig             a launch with no captured Triton variant runs the closest more general one
  zig/src/cuda/driver.zig          the driver's entry points resolved after cuInit; entry points the family uses
  zig/src/cuda/kernels.zig         the family's kernel modules
  zig/src/cuda/launch.zig          launch helpers the family uses
  zig/src/cuda/nccl.zig            NCCL send/recv entry points
  zig/src/native/cuda.zig          the dsv41 family registered with the native server (efforts, images, kept prompts)
  zig/src/server/chat.zig          image content parts; return_token_ids puts the reply's ids in its tensorfold block
  zig/src/server/hf_text.zig       an engine's reasoning-effort numbers
  zig/src/server/messages.zig      image parts: data URLs, every image format and the refusals
  zig/src/server/model_text.zig    an engine's reasoning-effort numbers
  zig/src/server/openai.zig        image parts and return_token_ids
  zig/src/server/prompt.zig        image prompts; reasoning-effort numbers
  zig/src/server/reply_text.zig    DSML tool calls
  zig/src/server/root.zig          the tool-call parser's module
  zig/src/server/server.zig        an engine's reasoning-effort numbers
  zig/src/server/tool_parse.zig    DSML tool calls
  zig/src/server/tool_parse_test.zig   tests for them
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md           the DeepSeek-V4.1 section

The "git log" of this branch and tools/dsv41-zig/ATTRIBUTION.md describe the changes and their sources.

Frontend adaptation, 2026-10-24:
Port MiaAI-Lab patches 0027 and 0028 by Coinupbtc and 0029 by Maciej Kowalik.
Adapt the control masking to this tokenizer, include rendered schema keys and decoded tool arguments, and
isolate legacy SSE-history newline repair. CREDITS.md records source commits.

Prompt preparation memory work from Robert Wojciechowski, Mia patch 0023,
adapted while preserving frontend control-token masking. Apache-2.0.

TP3 failure recovery adapts the bounded exit/restart idea in Robert
Wojciechowski's Mia 0020; it does not import the TP2 spill/rank-wire series.
DeepSeek optional context capacity includes Robert Wojciechowski's GLM-to-DeepSeek
port, BadAd84's spill v2 design, and MiaAI-Lab recipe adaptations from commit
2fd7809571e4d34f46a055dabf11caed9b145988. Modified here for TP3, K2a cache
compatibility, native Responses token counting and fail-closed launch checks.
